30-generator-contract: the generator of curry.eval.

Seam: laziness, next and its default, break and close, failure as no value,
an error and a suspension in the stream.
Sources: memo A6, A12; catalogue P27, P42, P46; Using the API, "Multi-Valued
Computations".  Backends: py, cxx.  Oracle: oracle.out, the PAKCS 3.4.1 REPL
on three, mixed, nothing, x + 1 =:= 3 and the choice of a value and a
suspension.

Expected output: curry.eval returns Results and runs nothing; next gives
1; a for loop that breaks after 2 keeps the search, so the next value is 3,
then StopIteration; after close() the list is empty.  The failed goal
nothing gives the default None and the empty list, where PAKCS prints
"*** No value found!" and exits 2 (P46).  mixed gives 1, then the
EvaluationError boom ends the stream and the 2 never comes (P27); PAKCS
prints 1 and ERROR: boom.  x + 1 =:= 3 with x free suspends on the rigid +
and raises SuspensionError with the goal text, under EvaluationError; PAKCS prints
"*** Evaluation suspended!".  The choice of x =:= 1 with the suspension
gives True first and then the suspension in either order of the operands,
in step mode on both backends.  Pins no defect.
